1
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,499
Let's skip training today.

2
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,250
You were hurt pretty badly.

3
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:20,839
No, my injuries pose no problem.

4
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:24,629
I am more concerned about
you, Shirou. Are you all right?

5
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:26,640
Yeah, I'm okay.

6
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:31,100
If you are in pain, do
not hesitate to speak up.

7
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:32,640
Sure.

8
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:11,270
In the face of absolute despair

9
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:15,270
That nearly burned
our hearts away

10
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:21,820
You still found the
courage to smile

11
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:26,620
Like you accepted it all

12
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,880
I lost my voice

13
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:32,500
And the things I wanted to say

14
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:37,750
But every time I
fell to my knees

15
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:42,050
I stood up and kept walking

16
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:47,720
We were looking for
the ideal white future

17
00:01:47,930 --> 00:01:52,950
Our one and only hope

18
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,440
Now I may be left with nothing

19
00:01:55,610 --> 00:02:00,860
But these raging
emotions that have

20
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,960
Nowhere to go

21
00:02:04,210 --> 00:02:09,210
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

22
00:02:09,590 --> 00:02:12,620
With more than one right answer

23
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:16,450
I won't stop

24
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:18,480
Until I find it

25
00:02:25,170 --> 00:02:29,510
A Visitor Approaches Lightly

26
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:41,020
That's a relief.
The pain is gone.

27
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,030
Yesterday was
pretty rough, I guess.

28
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:58,080
I think I'll make
breakfast as thanks.

29
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,960
Shirou?

30
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:18,310
So, Kuzuki-sensei
has called in sick today.

31
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:20,599
Seriously? Kuzuki-sensei?

32
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,809
Did Hell freeze over?

33
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:24,310
Sweet! Study hall!

34
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:24,310
Settle down, everyone.

35
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:27,729
I know that normally this
is your world history class,

36
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:32,450
but now that I'm here, let's
have an English pop quiz!

37
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:34,359
No quizzes!

38
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,699
Tyrant!

39
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,869
Tiger!

40
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:38,199
Shut up!

41
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:42,789
If I make last period on Saturday
study hall, it might as well be playtime!

42
00:03:42,790 --> 00:03:46,330
So graciously accept
your teacher's kindness!

43
00:03:54,050 --> 00:03:55,340
School has now ended.

44
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:59,469
Students are not permitted to
remain on campus after school hours.

45
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:01,390
Please return home at once.

46
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:05,899
Should I be worried?

47
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,730
I'm not feeling any pain, but
my arm feels heavier somehow.

48
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:13,110
I forgot to talk to Tohsaka.

49
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:19,240
Well, if she didn't come to me, I doubt
there were any major developments.

50
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:26,709
Sorry I'm home late.

51
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:29,090
I'll have lunch
ready in a minute.

52
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:34,719
Shirou?

53
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,470
That's the first time
I've ever broken a dish.

54
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,059
Sorry. I'll clean
it up right away.

55
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:44,020
Don't worry about
it. Just sit at the table.

56
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:47,600
You must be fatigued, Shirou.

57
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:51,020
It's all right. I
will clean it up.

58
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:55,280
Yeah, maybe I am. Thanks.

59
00:04:59,200 --> 00:04:59,950
All right!

60
00:04:59,951 --> 00:05:01,450
Coming!

61
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,509
T-Tohsaka? What
are you doing here?

62
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:16,719
I'm here because you stood
me up at our regular check-in.

63
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,129
Stood you up?

64
00:05:18,130 --> 00:05:21,140
Okay, I admit that I
forgot to meet you.

65
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:24,640
But when did we ever
decide on regular check-ins?

66
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:29,099
Sorry! I'm sorry for forgetting!

67
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:32,479
You're right. As partners,
we should check in regularly.

68
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:35,280
Let's use this opportunity to
hold our meeting here today.

69
00:05:36,490 --> 00:05:39,359
Hang on! We were
just about to have lunch!

70
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,779
Perfect timing, then.

71
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,490
I haven't had lunch yet,

72
00:05:42,910 --> 00:05:44,080
so I'll join you.

73
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,500
Hey! Not so fast!

74
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:58,929
So in the end, our only option
against Caster is to attack her head-on.

75
00:05:58,930 --> 00:06:00,429
I believe so.

76
00:06:00,430 --> 00:06:02,662
There is a powerful
barrier against spiritual

77
00:06:02,674 --> 00:06:04,469
beings erected
around that mountain.

78
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:06,310
The front gate is the only way.

79
00:06:06,730 --> 00:06:11,690
So if we force our way in to the
temple grounds, Caster will be waiting.

80
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:13,149
I suppose so.

81
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:16,779
Wait, why are you
sitting so far away?

82
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:20,070
Because you stole
my usual place!

83
00:06:22,030 --> 00:06:26,660
Anyway, once we're on the grounds,
the question is how we'll corner Caster.

84
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:30,959
Worst case scenario, she might
take out all of Ryuudou Temple.

85
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:33,539
True, that is something
Caster could do.

86
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:36,759
Saber, don't say scary
stuff like that so casually!

87
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:39,799
Are you saying that Caster will
self-destruct if we corner her?

88
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:41,380
It's likely, yes.

89
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:43,510
I believe she would.

90
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:49,480
You two are totally in sync.

91
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,110
Wow, when did it get this late?

92
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,399
I guess we should
wrap things up.

93
00:06:57,400 --> 00:07:00,280
I need to get dinner started.

94
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:04,199
What is it, Emiya-kun?

95
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:06,409
Why are you staring at me?

96
00:07:06,410 --> 00:07:08,329
No, I was just...

97
00:07:08,330 --> 00:07:10,959
Oh, I get it.

98
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:14,329
In public, we're fellow Masters,
so I don't bother you there,

99
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:16,039
but inside your own home,

100
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:18,170
you revert to your
natural instincts.

101
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:22,260
I'm a guy, so it's a
perfectly ordinary reaction.

102
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:24,389
But don't you
think it's strange?

103
00:07:24,390 --> 00:07:26,429
I mean, Saber's a girl.

104
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:30,140
And from what I hear, Fujimura-sensei
and Sakura are always coming over.

105
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:33,269
I shouldn't be any different.

106
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:35,399
Look, just go home, okay?

107
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:39,570
Oh? How can I go home when
we've yet to settle on a strategy?

108
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:43,949
Shirou, Rin's point
is valid, is it not?

109
00:07:43,950 --> 00:07:47,240
I see no issue with
her staying here.

110
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,120
Don't you start too.

111
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:52,119
All right, fine.

112
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:55,999
But Fuji-nee—Fujimura-sensei
will probably show up later,

113
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,379
so if anything, you should
worry about convincing her.

114
00:07:58,380 --> 00:08:00,589
I know, I know.

115
00:08:00,590 --> 00:08:01,990
I was aware I'd
have to deal with

116
00:08:02,002 --> 00:08:03,970
Fujimura-sensei from
the start. It'll be fine.

117
00:08:05,090 --> 00:08:07,390
Well, don't blame me if
this blows up in your face.

118
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,809
I'm home!

119
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:13,059
Welcome back.

120
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,809
Boy, it's cold!

121
00:08:14,810 --> 00:08:16,770
I think it's gonna snow!

122
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:19,479
Ah, you're making hot pot!

123
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,479
That's my Shirou!

124
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,609
You're freezing!

125
00:08:21,610 --> 00:08:24,030
You always know just what to do!

126
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:24,029
Be careful!

127
00:08:24,030 --> 00:08:25,610
I'm working over a fire here!

128
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:26,989
Whatever! Hurry, hurry, hurry!

129
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:31,790
Hot pot! Hot pot! Hot pot!

130
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,330
Come on, get off me!

131
00:08:31,790 --> 00:08:34,039
I hope you don't mind my
joining you, Fujimura-sensei.

132
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:36,579
Why, it's Tohsaka-san!

133
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:40,670
It's rare to see you
at Shirou's—hang on.

134
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:44,670
What's Tohsaka doing here?

135
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:47,219
Hang on, Tohsaka-san!

136
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:49,179
What are you doing
here at this hour?

137
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:51,139
Don't you have any common sense?

138
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:52,469
What am I doing here?

139
00:08:52,470 --> 00:08:55,810
I'm being treated to
dinner at Emiya-kun's place.

140
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:59,450
I think it takes even less
common sense for you to barge

141
00:08:59,462 --> 00:09:02,480
in without even ringing the
doorbell, wouldn't you say?

142
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:07,109
I-I'm the household chaperone!

143
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:10,239
Emiya-kun's father
left me in charge,

144
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,680
so I'm basically
part of the family!

145
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:13,749
Oh, I see.

146
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:16,709
Emiya-kun and I will be
studying for a test after dinner,

147
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:18,375
so don't mind us.

148
00:09:18,376 --> 00:09:19,880
Ouch...

149
00:09:19,881 --> 00:09:21,379
Shirou? I mean, Emiya-kun!

150
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:22,999
What's the meaning of this?

151
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:27,049
Don't force yourself to use his
surname if you're not used to it.

152
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:31,600
What you call Emiya-kun
is none of my concern.

153
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:35,849
Tohsaka-san, did you hear
about this from Sakura-chan?

154
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:36,850
Who knows?

155
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:42,609
Unfortunately, anything that Matou-san
told me must be treated as confidential.

156
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:46,360
But I hope it's
exactly as you think.

157
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:49,240
Game, set, and match.

158
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:54,409
I'll leave these here.

159
00:09:54,410 --> 00:09:55,410
Oh, thanks.

160
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,789
Shall I do the dishes?

161
00:09:57,790 --> 00:10:00,646
It wouldn't be fair for me to eat your
food without lifting a finger to help.

162
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:02,880
Nah. You can just
owe me for next time.

163
00:10:19,270 --> 00:10:22,689
Fujimura-sensei, is
Emiya-kun always this clumsy?

164
00:10:22,690 --> 00:10:23,690
No way.

165
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:27,740
He's never broken a dish before
for as long as I can remember.

166
00:10:28,070 --> 00:10:31,529
He's probably self-conscious
because you're here.

167
00:10:31,530 --> 00:10:33,570
As in, he's thrown off by
the unexpected intrusion.

168
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:38,330
Emiya-kun.

169
00:10:38,331 --> 00:10:41,079
I'll take it from here,
so go get some rest.

170
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:42,209
No, I couldn't...

171
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:45,420
I've got this. Go
drink some tea.

172
00:10:49,590 --> 00:10:51,180
Are you okay with not helping?

173
00:10:51,590 --> 00:10:54,549
You asked her over, so if you leave
her alone, she's gonna hate you.

174
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:56,969
Wh-Why are you reading
so far into this, you idiot?

175
00:10:56,970 --> 00:10:59,430
And I didn't invite her over!

176
00:10:59,770 --> 00:11:04,230
Besides, I don't really
care if Tohsaka hates me.

177
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:14,410
Huh? Where's Tohsaka?

178
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:17,160
I believe she went
out into the courtyard.

179
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:19,120
The courtyard?

180
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,090
Tohsaka?

181
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:29,880
I like the magic field here.

182
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,890
Unlike the one at my house, you
can sense human warmth in this one.

183
00:11:39,930 --> 00:11:41,180
Care to join me?

184
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,569
What?

185
00:11:51,570 --> 00:11:53,609
I was just curious.

186
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:55,739
This house is unique.

187
00:11:55,740 --> 00:12:01,119
It occurred to me that maybe
you're better off the way you are.

188
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:03,620
A hopeless amateur, you mean?

189
00:12:04,210 --> 00:12:07,289
I didn't mean it that way,
but maybe that's exactly it.

190
00:12:07,290 --> 00:12:11,209
I don't know what Emiya
Kiritsugu was like as a mage,

191
00:12:11,210 --> 00:12:14,010
but this estate is
incredibly laid-back.

192
00:12:14,510 --> 00:12:17,429
For a mage's
workshop, it's quite open.

193
00:12:17,430 --> 00:12:20,679
It's like you're welcome
to come and go freely.

194
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:23,060
It isn't like that
at your place?

195
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:25,309
No, it isn't.

196
00:12:25,310 --> 00:12:29,440
It tries to keep people out, but
once you're in, it doesn't let you leave.

197
00:12:31,230 --> 00:12:36,859
At times, I think it's messed up,
but it isn't something I can change.

198
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,990
Personally, I like
it the way it is.

199
00:12:40,910 --> 00:12:44,960
This personality of mine is probably
why I was chosen as the heir.

200
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:48,579
Was it hard for you?

201
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,799
Training to be a mage?

202
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:54,589
Sorry to say, but I
never had much trouble.

203
00:12:54,590 --> 00:12:58,259
Plus, learning
new things was fun.

204
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:02,060
Didn't I just tell you?
That's how I'm wired.

205
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:06,190
So if you're worried
about me, don't be.

206
00:13:07,810 --> 00:13:08,810
Okay.

207
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,479
So why do you go to school?

208
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,779
If you're going to live a mage's
life, isn't it sort of pointless?

209
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:17,779
It may be somewhat of a
detour, but it's not pointless.

210
00:13:17,780 --> 00:13:20,029
It's fun to be a student.

211
00:13:20,030 --> 00:13:23,080
And at heart, having
fun's what I live for.

212
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:26,329
Succeeding my father is my duty,

213
00:13:26,330 --> 00:13:29,000
but I wouldn't do
it if I didn't enjoy it.

214
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:32,960
That's even why I partnered with
you. Because you're fun to be around.

215
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,799
I see.

216
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,839
Well, I'm glad
you're having fun.

217
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,509
Thanks.

218
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:41,850
And? It's been fun
for you too, right?

219
00:13:44,270 --> 00:13:46,639
Why aren't you saying anything?

220
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,940
Well, I just...

221
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,229
Give me a straight
answer, Emiya-kun.

222
00:13:55,230 --> 00:13:58,570
Because I might have
completely misunderstood you.

223
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:04,659
Well... I guess I never
thought of mage training as fun.

224
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:06,290
Or even magic itself.

225
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:11,170
But if the people around
me were happy, I was happy.

226
00:14:12,170 --> 00:14:17,510
So I figured if I studied magic, I might
be able to help someone someday.

227
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:22,549
I wanted to be a champion
of justice, just like Kiritsugu.

228
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:24,849
That's why I did it.

229
00:14:24,850 --> 00:14:28,389
Anyway, that's my reason.

230
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:32,440
So what are you saying? You
didn't study magic for yourself?

231
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,779
I didn't?

232
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:40,239
I mean, it makes me happy
to be useful to others, so...

233
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,989
No, listen here! That's just
being happy, not having fun!

234
00:14:43,990 --> 00:14:48,789
Look, what I'm asking is
if you personally enjoy it.

235
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:50,419
I don't care about other people.

236
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:53,710
I'm asking if there's anything
about magic that you consider fun!

237
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:57,960
I don't know if I
personally enjoy it.

238
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:03,211
I guess I feel like I
don't have the right

239
00:15:03,223 --> 00:15:05,509
to ask for more than
I've been given already.

240
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:06,390
Hey!

241
00:15:06,391 --> 00:15:07,769
Give me a straight answer!

242
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:09,480
Well... I suppose I don't.

243
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,439
Man, this ticks me off!

244
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,809
So basically,

245
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:18,029
you're always worrying about
others but never focusing on yourself!

246
00:15:18,030 --> 00:15:18,990
Whoa, hey...

247
00:15:18,991 --> 00:15:20,699
Shut up! No talking back!

248
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:26,779
I always thought you were similar,
but I never imagined you were this alike!

249
00:15:26,780 --> 00:15:28,869
Calm down, Tohsaka.

250
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:31,119
I don't understand
why you're so angry.

251
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:34,040
That's exactly why I'm angry!

252
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:37,750
All right. That settles it.

253
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:42,179
Tomorrow, I'll make
you admit defeat!

254
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,470
You're going to go back
to chasing me around?

255
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,099
You bet!

256
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:49,220
I'll give you a taste of something
special I've been saving!

257
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:56,770
Hey, Tohsaka!

258
00:15:57,110 --> 00:15:59,319
You're going home, right?

259
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,779
I'll walk you.

260
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:01,900
Tohsaka!

261
00:16:05,990 --> 00:16:08,739
Enough with the
"Tohsaka, Tohsaka"!

262
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:10,829
Tohsaka, what are you wearing?

263
00:16:10,830 --> 00:16:14,619
I spoke to Archer and had
him bring me an overnight bag.

264
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:15,120
Huh?

265
00:16:15,121 --> 00:16:17,960
I got Fujimura-sensei's
permission, so it's fine.

266
00:16:19,090 --> 00:16:21,590
I'll use the guest
room on the right.

267
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:33,350
Trace on.

268
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:37,769
Tracing fundamental structure.

269
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:40,150
Reinforcing
auxiliary components.

270
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,490
More magic training tonight?

271
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:55,500
Yeah. Kiritsugu taught
me to never miss a day.

272
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,750
But I guess that was the only
thing I really learned from him.

273
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:01,840
Only that?

274
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:07,130
He taught you nothing of the wisdom
or behavior expected of mages?

275
00:17:07,550 --> 00:17:09,429
Nah. After all,

276
00:17:09,430 --> 00:17:13,059
despite being my teacher, he
wasn't much of a mage himself.

277
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:14,640
He was a poor
excuse for an adult.

278
00:17:15,270 --> 00:17:16,848
He'd say that if you
were going to enjoy

279
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,689
something, you should
enjoy it to the fullest,

280
00:17:18,690 --> 00:17:20,650
and then he'd play
around like a kid.

281
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:25,649
I understand. You enjoyed
having such a master, didn't you?

282
00:17:25,650 --> 00:17:27,859
Yeah. I looked up to him.

283
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:30,579
He was carefree and
not at all mage-like,

284
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:34,540
but to me, Kiritsugu
was a true magician.

285
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:38,540
Shirou.

286
00:17:38,830 --> 00:17:41,380
What is wrong
with your left side?

287
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:45,630
You noticed?

288
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:46,920
Yes.

289
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,799
It's just a little numb.

290
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:52,260
It isn't slowing me down at all.

291
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:54,220
Is the cause what I think it is?

292
00:17:54,890 --> 00:17:58,890
Yeah, I think it's a reaction to
the projection magic I did last night.

293
00:18:00,690 --> 00:18:03,110
Is your body still half-numb?

294
00:18:03,570 --> 00:18:04,819
Archer.

295
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:06,740
That's hardly surprising.

296
00:18:07,610 --> 00:18:09,409
What do you want, Archer?

297
00:18:09,410 --> 00:18:12,910
I thought we had a
non-aggression pact.

298
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,160
Stop right there.

299
00:18:15,161 --> 00:18:18,580
If you come any closer, I hope you're
prepared to face the consequences.

300
00:18:18,910 --> 00:18:21,749
Wait, Saber. He
doesn't want to fight.

301
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:22,500
But...

302
00:18:22,501 --> 00:18:23,839
It's okay.

303
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:26,509
What do you want, Archer?

304
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:29,680
Knowing you, I'm guessing you
didn't just drop by to say hello.

305
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:34,680
Rin told me that you performed
a projection, and it really is true.

306
00:18:35,350 --> 00:18:37,807
You have no sensation
in half your body, and your

307
00:18:37,819 --> 00:18:40,440
center of gravity is seven
centimeters off, correct?

308
00:18:41,770 --> 00:18:43,650
I may be able to assist you.

309
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,989
You're fortunate.

310
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:52,949
I expected to see necrosis,

311
00:18:52,950 --> 00:18:55,190
but you've simply opened
something that was once closed.

312
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:58,000
I've opened something
that was once closed?

313
00:18:58,410 --> 00:19:02,500
The circuits you were meant to use from the
beginning had grown dormant from neglect.

314
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,539
The numbness is only temporary.

315
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:09,919
By suddenly flooding circuits you
never used with mana at full power,

316
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:13,549
you sent them into
a state of shock.

317
00:19:13,550 --> 00:19:16,810
This means that the circuits
have returned to an active state.

318
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:24,980
That should do it.

319
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,730
You'll recover in a few days.

320
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,859
When you can
move properly again,

321
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:33,700
you'll find yourself a
better mage than before.

322
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:37,030
You certainly know a
lot about this, Archer.

323
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:40,039
I went through
something similar.

324
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,710
At first, I lost the
use of one arm.

325
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:46,090
Wait.

326
00:19:47,210 --> 00:19:48,460
What?

327
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:52,760
I want to ask you something.

328
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:55,929
"Let your ideals drag
you to your death."

329
00:19:55,930 --> 00:19:58,310
What did you mean by that?

330
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,469
It seems self-explanatory.

331
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:02,480
There's nothing to add.

332
00:20:03,190 --> 00:20:06,189
Then what the hell
are you fighting for?

333
00:20:06,190 --> 00:20:11,569
That's obvious. I fight
for myself—simple as that.

334
00:20:11,570 --> 00:20:13,899
Just for yourself?

335
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:15,279
That's right.

336
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:19,289
If you desire to fulfill your
ideal of nobody getting hurt,

337
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:20,949
then so be it.

338
00:20:20,950 --> 00:20:24,790
But only if that
desire is truly yours.

339
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:28,709
If you fight of
your own free will,

340
00:20:28,710 --> 00:20:32,509
you bring the
consequences upon yourself.

341
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:34,720
Accepting them is
a part of that ideal.

342
00:20:35,050 --> 00:20:38,509
But if that desire was
borrowed from another,

343
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:41,850
the ideals you uphold
are mere fantasies.

344
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,519
One must have a
reason for fighting.

345
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:47,149
But that reason must
never be an ideal.

346
00:20:47,150 --> 00:20:51,110
If you fight for an ideal,
you can only save ideals.

347
00:20:52,570 --> 00:20:55,490
And that means
you can't help others.

348
00:20:56,740 --> 00:21:00,659
All reasons to fight
involve saving something.

349
00:21:00,660 --> 00:21:03,910
Or at the very least, yours
does. Is that right, Emiya Shirou?

350
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:08,540
But salvation by the hands
of another is not salvation.

351
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:12,459
Such salvation is like money.

352
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:14,880
When used, it passes
into another's hands.

353
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:19,639
It's true that you can probably
achieve your desire to save others.

354
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:23,969
But you have no
desire to save yourself.

355
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:27,226
You will repeat the
cycle until you die, still

356
00:21:27,238 --> 00:21:30,150
clinging to ideals
that are not your own.

357
00:21:32,070 --> 00:21:35,900
That is why your
ideals are meaningless.

358
00:21:38,410 --> 00:21:40,869
Nothing comes of helping others.

359
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:44,370
In the end, you can save
neither others nor yourself.

360
00:21:44,950 --> 00:21:46,960
A lie of a life.

361
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,040
You're wrong.

362
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:55,130
That isn't true.

363
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:16,539
We didn't understand anything

364
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:22,709
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

365
00:22:22,710 --> 00:22:25,709
A moral conflict

366
00:22:25,710 --> 00:22:28,510
stays your hand

367
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,259
and tricks you

368
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:33,140
out of your future

369
00:22:33,390 --> 00:22:40,059
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

370
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:45,860
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

371
00:22:46,070 --> 00:22:54,070
but I want to live my life

372
00:22:55,070 --> 00:23:00,079
The past repeats before my eyes

373
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:07,879
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

374
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:13,969
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

375
00:23:13,970 --> 00:23:19,599
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

376
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:23,310
Fight your fate

377
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:29,929
You don't have to go to
such extremes to help others!

378
00:23:29,930 --> 00:23:31,769
You truly are a foolish child!

379
00:23:31,770 --> 00:23:34,359
You still have no stomach
for brutality, do you?

380
00:23:34,360 --> 00:23:37,649
I promised myself that I'd
fight to stop people like you.

381
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:38,755
Run, Shirou!

382
00:23:38,756 --> 00:23:40,990
The Final Decision

383
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:40,990
Next Time

